  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nSpecifically, in the [HTML fragment parsing algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parsing-html-fragments), step 1 creates a temporary Document  \"`document`\", that is used for parsing.\n> 1. Let document be a Document node whose type is \"html\".\n\nBy default its custom element registry is null. I believe it should be set here to the context element's document's custom element registry.\n\nThe effect of not doing this, is that when created elements get adopted into `document`, step 3.1.3.2 of [adopt node](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt) overwrites it:\n\n> 2. If inclusiveDescendant’s [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-custom-element-registry) is null or inclusiveDescendant’s [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-custom-element-registry)’s [is scoped](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#is-scoped) is false, then set inclusiveDescendant’s [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-custom-element-registry) to document’s [effective global custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#effective-global-custom-element-registry).\n\nThe document here is `document`, which as explained above has a null custom element registry, so the element's gets set to null too. If `document` has the same registry as the \"real\" document, then this functions as expected instead.",
